.TH NOARK5\-TG\-MCP 1 "August 2026" "noark5-tg-mcp 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
noark5-tg-mcp \- Model Context Protocol server for Noark 5 tjenestegrensesnitt API
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B noark5-tg-mcp
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBnoark5\-tg\-mcp\fR is an MCP (Model Context Protocol) server that provides tools
for browsing, searching, and managing archive entities through the Noark 5
tjenestegrensesnitt REST API. It supports authentication via Basic auth or OIDC/OAuth2,
HATEOAS endpoint discovery, CRUD operations on all major entity types, and OData
search/filter across collections.
.PP
The server exposes MCP tools that can be used by LLM\-powered applications such as
Claude Desktop or opencode to interact with a Noark 5 archive system.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help message and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-base-url \fIURL\fR
API base URL (overrides the \fBNOARK5_BASE_URL\fR environment variable).
.TP
.B \-\-list-tools
List all available MCP tools with descriptions and exit. Useful for discovering
what functionality is available without starting the server.
.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
The following environment variables configure the server's behavior:
.TP
.I NOARK5_BASE_URL
API base URL (default: \fBhttp://localhost:8092/noark5v5/\fR).
.TP
.I NOARK5_USERNAME
Authentication username for Basic or OIDC login.
.TP
.I NOARK5_PASSWORD
Authentication password (required together with \fBNOARK5_USERNAME\fR).
.TP
.I NOARK5_AUTH_METHOD
Authentication method: \fBauto\fR, \fBbasic\fR, or \fBoidc\fR (default: \fBauto\fR).
With \fBauto\fR, the server queries the API root entity to detect available login
endpoints and prefers OIDC over Basic auth.
.TP
.I NOARK5_CLIENT_ID
OIDC client identifier (optional, used with the \fBoidc\fR method).
.TP
.I NOARK5_ACCESS_TOKEN
Pre\-existing access token. If set, the server skips the login flow entirely and
uses this token for authentication.
.SH MCP TOOLS
The server provides 33+ tools covering:
.IP \(bu
Authentication and credential management (\fBnoark5_set_credentials\fR)
.IP \(bu
Entity listing (arkiv, arkivdel, mappe, registrering, klasse, saksmappe, etc.)
.IP \(bu
Entity creation, update (merge PATCH), and deletion
.IP \(bu
OData search and filtering across collections
.IP \(bu
HATEOAS navigation (\fBnoark5_entity_links\fR, \fBnoark5_list_parents\fR)
.IP \(bu
File download from dokumentobjekt and upload to dokumentbeskrivelse
.IP \(bu
Secondary entity creation (forfatter, noekkelord, merknad, etc.)
.PP
Run \fBnoark5\-tg\-mcp \-\-list-tools\fR for a complete listing.
.SH USAGE WITH CLAUDE DESKTOP
Add the following to your \fIclaude_desktop_config.json\fR:
.IP
.EX
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "noark5": {
      "command": "noark5-tg-mcp",
      "env": {
        "NOARK5_BASE_URL": "http://localhost:8092/noark5v5/",
        "NOARK5_USERNAME": "your-username",
        "NOARK5_PASSWORD": "your-password"
      }
    }
  }
}
.EE
.SH USAGE WITH OPencode
Add the following to your \fI~/.config/opencode/opencode.jsonc\fR:
.IP
.EX
{
  "mcp": {
    "noark5": {
      "type": "local",
      "command": ["noark5-tg-mcp"],
      "environment": {
        "NOARK5_BASE_URL": "http://localhost:8092/noark5v5/",
        "NOARK5_USERNAME": "your-username",
        "NOARK5_PASSWORD": "your-password"
      },
      "enabled": true
    }
  }
}
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful execution.
.TP
.B non-zero
An error occurred (e.g., failed authentication, network error).
.SH SEE ALSO
.RS
